$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM PREPARATION OF PHENOXIDE Phenol and substituted phenols (1 mmol) were
dissolved in aqueous sodium hydroxide solution (1.2 mmol) and stirred for
2 h at room-temperature. Water was evaporated under reduced pressure to
get solid phenoxides. PREPARATION OF DIARYLOXYMETHANES A mixture of
phenoxides (2 mmol) and dichloromethane (1 mmol) was stirred in ionic
liquid [bmim] Br (5 mL) at 60°C for an appropriate time period as shown
in Table 2. Completion of the reaction was monitored by thin-layer
chromatography using 5% ethyl acetate in petroleum ether. The reaction
mixture was diluted with water (20 mL) and then extracted with ethyl
acetate (3 x 10 mL). The separated organic layer was dried over anhydrous
sodium sulfate, and the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure to
afford the diaryloxymethanes. The product was purified by column
chromatography using 5% ethyl acetate in petroleum ether as an eluent.
The ionic liquid was extracted from the aqueous layer with
dichloromethane (3 x 10 mL) and dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate, and
the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure leaving behind the
ionic liquid [bmim] Br, which could be recycled. Table 2, Entry 1, yield
90%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, Williamson's synthesis, ionic liquid used, yield
depends on number of solvent reuse cycles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Room-Temperature Ionic Liquid-Promoted Williamson Synthesis of Ethers: A
Facile Synthesis of Diaryloxymethanes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
