$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: PREPARATION OF PHENOXIDE Phenol and
substituted phenols (1 mmol) were dissolved in aqueous sodium hydroxide
solution (1.2 mmol) and stirred for 2 h at room-temperature. Water was
evaporated under reduced pressure to get solid phenoxides. PREPARATION OF
DIARYLOXYMETHANES A mixture of phenoxides (2 mmol) and dichloromethane (1
mmol) was stirred in ionic liquid [bmim] Br (5 mL) at 60°C for an
appropriate time period as shown in Table 2. Completion of the reaction
was monitored by thin-layer chromatography using 5% ethyl acetate in
petroleum ether. The reaction mixture was diluted with water (20 mL) and
then extracted with ethyl acetate (3 x 10 mL). The separated organic
layer was dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate, and the solvent was
evaporated under reduced pressure to afford the diaryloxymethanes. The
product was purified by column chromatography using 5% ethyl acetate in
petroleum ether as an eluent. The ionic liquid was extracted from the
aqueous layer with dichloromethane (3 x 10 mL) and dried over anhydrous
sodium sulfate, and the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
leaving behind the ionic liquid [bmim] Br, which could be recycled. Table
2, Entry 6, yield 90%. Mp (°C): 7012]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, Williamson's synthesis, ionic liquid used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Room-Temperature Ionic Liquid-Promoted Williamson Synthesis of Ethers: A
Facile Synthesis of Diaryloxymethanes
