$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3,3’’’-Dibenzyloxy triply-bridged quaternaphthalene (R,S,R)-and (R,R,R)-8
The preparation of (R,S,R)-8 is typical. A suspension of (R,S,R)-7 (330
mg, 393 µmol), bromochloromethane (1.06 ml, 11.8 mmol) and potassium
carbonate (543 mg, 3.93 mmol) in DMF (10 ml) was stirred for 7 hours at
50 °C. The reaction mixture was poured into the mixed solvent of
chloroform and water. The organic layer was separated and washed
successively with 0.1 N hydrochloric acid solution (twice), water (twice)
and brine. After dried over sodium sulfate, the solvent was evaporated in
vacuo to give a residue. The residue was purified by column
chromatography (SiO2; n-hexane/chloroform/ethyl acetate = 5/3/1) to
afford (R,S,R)-7 (334 mg, 393 µmol, >99%). (R,S,R)-8; yellow solid; mp.
221-223 °C; [α]D20= -296 (CHCl3, c 0.10); IR (KBr pellet method) 3065,
2898, 1596, 1453, 1406, 1243 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.42 (AB q,
J = 12.4 Hz, Δν = 9.5 Hz, 4H), 5.95 (AB q, J = 3.2 Hz, Δν = 24.8 Hz, 4H),
6.00 (s, 2H), 7.2-8.0 (m, 28H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 70.6, 103.5,
104.0, 110.1, 124.1, 125.4, 125.5, 125.7, 126.7, 127.0, 127.3, 127.6,
127.8, 128.0, 128.4, 128.6, 128.6, 128.8, 130.0, 130.2, 132.2, 136.6,
142.9, 144.5, 144.7, 150.1; HRMS (FAB+) Calcd for C57H38O8 (M)+:
850.2567. Found: 850.2596; LR MS (FAB+) 850.3 (M)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Multibridged Chiral Naphthalene Oligomers with Continuous Extreme-Cisoid
