$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Preparation of Benzyl
Phenyl Ether (Entry 1). A mixture of phenol (0.47 g, 5 mmol), benzyl
chloride (0.75 g, 6 mmol), KOH (0.41 g, 82%, 6 mmol) and BMImPF6 (4 mL)
in a 20 mL round bottomed flask fitted with mechanical stirrer, was
stirred at room temperature and the reaction was monitored by thin layer
chromatography (TLC, silica gel 254, eluted hexane-ethyl acetate, 2:1).
After all the phenol had been consumed, the reaction mixture was
extracted with ethyl ether (3 x 10 mL), the organic extract was washed,
dried, and the solvent was distilled off. Sr: 6; Yield 97%. bp.
280-282°C, lit. bp b282°C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
