$DATUM WILLIAMSON ETHER SYNTHESES. Metal alkoxides react with primary alkyl
halides to form ethers. This process is known as the Williamson ether
synthesis and is generally acknowledged as the best procedure for the
preparation of symmetrical and unsymmetrical ethers. Entry 33, yield 96%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Williamson reaction
