$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(2S,3S,4R)-2-azido-5(2-butyloxy)ethyloxy-3,4-O-isopropylidene-1-O-(2,3,4,6-tetra-O-benzyl-α-D-galactopyranosyl)pentan-1,3,4,5-tetraol
(15a). General Procedure for Alkylation of Compound 14. Under Ar
atmosphere, 0.135 mmol (100 mg) of 14 was dissolved in 1.5 mL of
anhydrous DMF and cooled to 0 °C; 0.20 mmol of NaH was added, and after
15 min, 0.160 mmol of alkyl bromide (or alkyl methanesulfonate) was added
dropwise. Solution was allowed to warm to rt and stirred overnight. The
reaction was quenched with 1 mL of an aqueous saturated solution of
NH4Cl. Solution was diluted with AcOEt and washed three times with water
and brine. After anhydrification with Na2SO4, the solvent was removed
under vacuum, and the product was purified by flash chromatography
(62-75% yield).
(2S,3S,4R)-2-azido-5(2-butyloxy)ethyloxy-3,4-O-isopropylidene-1-O-(2,3,4,6-tetra-O-benzyl-α-D-galactopyranosyl)pentan-1,3,4,5-tetraol
(15a).
(2S,3S,4R)-2-azido-5-O-dodecanyl-3,4-O-isopropylidene-1-O-(2,3,4,6-tetra-O-benzyl-α-D-galactopyranosyl)pentan-1,3,4,5-tetraol
(15d). The compound was obtained in 95% yield. Rf 0.52 (ETP/AcOEt = 8/2);
[α]Drt = + 36.1 (c = 1.0, CHCl3); 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.40-7.24 (m,
20H), 4.97-4.36 (m, 9H), 4.30 (s, 1H), 4.15-3.92 (m, 6H), 3.68 (m, 2H),
3.58-3.40 (m, 6H), 1.60 (m, 2H), 1.39 (s, 3H), 1.28 (s, 3H), 1.25 (m,
18H), 0.87 (m, 3H); 13C-NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 139.0, 138.7, 138.1,
128.4-127.6, 109.0, 98.9, 79.0, 76.2, 75.4, 74.8, 74.7, 73.5, 73.4, 73.0,
72.1, 70.0, 69.4, 69.2, 59.7, 32.0, 29.7-29.4, 27.9, 26.2, 25.6, 22.8,
14.2. Anal. Calcd. for C54H73N3O9: C, 71.42, H, 8.10, N, 4.63; Found C,
71.44, H, 8.37, N, 4.49.
