$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The diol (1.29 g, 4.33 mmol) and imidazole (383 mg, 5.63 mmol) were
dissolved in 20 mL CH2Cl2 and cooled to 0 °C. TBSCl (50 wt-% in toluene,
1.44 g, 4.76 mmol) was added dropwise and the mixture was stirred for 1 h
at rt. The excess TBSCl was trapped by the addition of MeOH (175 μL, 4.33
mmol) and after 30 min TBME (50 mL) was added. Aqueous workup using sat.
NaHCO3-solution and TBME (3 × 40 mL) and drying of the combined organic
layers with Na2SO4 followed by flash chromatography on silica neutralized
with Et3N (pentane/TBME 2:1) gave the secondary alcohol (1.67 g, 4.03
mmol, 93%) as a colorless oil. R f= 0.30 (PE/TBME 1:1). [α]D –4.23 (c =
1.18, CHCl3, ϑ 20°C). 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.37-7.26 (m, 5H),
4.67 (d, J = 11.5 Hz, 1H), 4.53 (d, J = 11.5 Hz, 1H), 4.38 (t, J = 5.5
Hz, 1H), 3.74 (t, J = 6.2 Hz, 1H), 3.60-3.46 (m, 2H), 3.32 (s, 3H), 3.31
(s, 3H), 2.69 (d, J = 5.4 Hz, 1H), 1.93-1.45 (m, 6H), 0.90 (s, 9H), 0.06
(s, 6H). 13C-NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 138.5, 128.4 (2C), 127.8 (2C),
127.7, 104.6, 79.5, 72.8, 72.7, 59.4, 52.9, 52.6, 33.9, 29.0, 28.2, 25.9
(3C), 18.2, –5.40, –5.42. HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd. for C22H40NaO5Si
(M+Na+): 435.2543, found: 435.2509.
