$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Septuply-bridged octinaphthalenes (R,S,R,S,R,S,R)-and (R,S,R,R,R,S,R)-10
A suspension of (R,S,R,S,R,S,R)-9 (15 mg, 9.9 µmol), bromochloromethane
(270 µl, 2.96 mmol) and potassium carbonate (14 mg, 99 µmol) in DMF (8.0
ml) was stirred for 24 hours at 50 °C. The reaction mixture was poured
into the mixed solvent of chloroform and water. The organic layer was
separated and washed successively with 0.1 N hydrochloric acid solution
(twice), water (twice) and brine. After dried over sodium sulfate, the
solvent was evaporated in vacuo to give a residue. The residue was
purified by column chromatography (SiO2; chloroform) to give a crude
material which was further purified by recycling preparative HPLC to
afford (R,S,R,S,R,S,R)-10 (14 mg, 9.1 μmol, 93%). (R,S,R,S,R,S,R)-10;
yellow solid. mp. >300 °C; [α]D20= -45 (CHCl3, c 0.10); IR (KBr pellet
method) 2901, 1596, 1404, 1093, 986 cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.40
(s, 4H), 5.8-6.1 (m, 14H), 7.2-7.9 (m, 44H); HRMS (ESI+) Calcd for
C101H63O16 (M+ H)+: 1531.4116. Found: 1531.4165; LR MS (FAB+) 1531.8 (M+
H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Multibridged Chiral Naphthalene Oligomers with Continuous Extreme-Cisoid
Conformation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Takaishi, Kazuto; Kawamoto, Masuki; Tsubaki, Kazunori
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2010), 12(8), 1832-1835

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME220 STEP1
