$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure for Preparation of Benzyl Phenyl Ether (Entry 1). A
mixture of phenol (0.47 g, 5 mmol), benzyl chloride (0.75 g, 6 mmol), KOH
(0.41 g, 82%, 6 mmol) and BMImPF6 (4 mL) in a 20 mL round bottomed flask
fitted with mechanical stirrer, was stirred at room temperature and the
reaction was monitored by thin layer chromatography (TLC, silica gel 254,
eluted hexane-ethyl acetate, 2:1). After all the phenol had been
consumed, the reaction mixture was extracted with ethyl ether (3 x 10
mL), the organic extract was washed, dried, and the solvent was distilled
off. 0.86 g (92%) of the desired product (purity 99% by GC). mp. 38-39°C,
lit.4 mp 39-41°C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, Williamson reaction, optimized on solvents
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Williamson reaction in ionic liquids
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Xu, Zhen Yuan; Xu, Dan Qian; Liu, Bao You
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Preparations and Procedures International (2004), 36(2), 156-161

