$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ethyl 2-[(2-ethoxy-2-oxoethoxy)methyl]quinoline-3-carboxylate (II) Ethyl
2-hydroxyacetate (10.4 g, 100 mmol) was added dropwise over 5 min to a
stirred solution of sodium ethoxide (3.74 g, 55 mmol) in absolute ethanol
(30 mL) and the reaction mixture was stirred at 50°C for 5 h. The solvent
was evaporated and the resulting sodium salt of ethyl 2-hydroxyacetate (a
white solid) was added to a solution of I (14.7 g, 50 mmol) in anhydrous
benzene (22 mL) and heated under reflux for 10 h (monitored by TLC). The
reaction was quenched with water and the product was extracted with Et2O.
The organic layer was dried with anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered and the
solvent evaporated to give the crude product; this was then purified by
flash chromatography on a column of silica gel (100-200 mesh) using
petroleum ether/EtOAc (ϕr = 10 : 1) as the eluent to afford II. White
solid, yield (14.1 g, 89 %). m.p. 57-58°C. IR, ν̃/ cm-1: 2983, 1761,
1714, 1566, 1442, 1276, 1132, 1065, 786. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3), δ: 1.27
(t, J= 7.1 Hz, 3H, COOCH2CH3), 1.45 (t, J= 7.1 Hz, 3H, COOCH2CH3), 4.21
(q, J= 7.1 Hz, 2H, COOCH2CH3), 4.29 (s, 2H, OCH2COO), 4.45 (q, J= 7.1 Hz,
2H, COOCH2CH3), 5.28 (s, 2H, ArCH2O), 7.58-7.61 (m, 1H, quinoline-H),
7.79-7.82 (m, 1H, quinoline-H), 7.89 (d, J= 8.2 Hz, 1H, quinoline- H),
8.16 (d, J= 8.4 Hz, 1H, quinoline-H), 8.73 (s, 1H, quinoline-H). 13C NMR
(150 MHz, CDCl3), δ: 14.19 (COOCH2CH3), 14.25 (COOCH2CH3), 60.78
(COOCH2CH3), 61.61 (COOCH2CH3), 68.52 (OCH2COOEt), 73.74 (ArCH2O),
123.62, 126.36, 127.37, 128.39, 129.45, 131.64, 139.88, 148.23, 156.35
(quinoline ring carbon atoms), 166.20 (COOEt), 170.22 (COOEt). ESI-MS,
m/z (Ir/%): 318.1 ([M + H]+, 25), 340.1 ([M + Na]+, 100). For C17H19NO5
(Mr = 317.34) wi/mass % calculated: C, 64.30; H, 6.03; N, 4.41; found: C,
64.52; H, 6.18; N, 4.34.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and keto-enol tautomerism of ethyl
4-oxo-3,4-dihydro-1H-pyrano[3,4-b]quinoline-3-carboxylate
